@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title House rules and UI defaults — proveo's conventions in every session, without touching a repository

' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, defs/claudecode/mcp/Dockerfile,
'         defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/themes/**
'
' Knobs: PROVEO_HOUSE_RULES=off · PROVEO_UI_DEFAULTS=off.
'
' ── 7g. UI DEFAULTS — A SANDBOX SHOULD LOOK LIKE A SANDBOX ─────────────────
' Two settings, both about reading the screen correctly, both claudecode-only
' because it is the only harness with a theme file proveo can write.
'
' THEME. A sandboxed session and a host session are the same program in the same
' terminal, and an operator with both open has nothing to tell them apart —
' which is how a command meant for the sandbox gets typed into the host. Claude
' Code supports custom themes as JSON under `<home>/.claude/themes/<slug>.json`,
' selected as `custom:<slug>`, so proveo ships one in its own identity palette:
' the accent, prompt border and permission dialogs go cyan/teal instead of the
' default orange. Visible at a glance, no reading required. The source is baked
' at /opt/proveo/themes/proveo-sandbox.json and COPIED into the agent home by
' the seed, so it reaches BOTH backends.
'
' SYNTAX HIGHLIGHTING is already Claude Code's default; `syntaxHighlightingDisabled
' = false` is written explicitly because the default is exactly the thing an
' inherited settings file can quietly flip, and a grep result rendered as flat
' text is materially harder to read.
'
' settings.json is MERGED, not written: the file is the operator's, only the two
' keys proveo has an opinion about are set, and each is set only when absent.
' The same file carries the cwd guard's PreToolUse hook
' (_spec/internal/sbx/virtiofs-cwd-invalidation.puml), so the merge discipline is
' shared rather than particular to the theme.

node "proveo image" as IMG <<host>> {
  file "/opt/proveo/AGENTS\.md\nthis repo's conventions, baked in" as SRC <<db>>
}

node "Managed policy path (baked, root-owned)" as MANAGED <<host>> {
  file "claudecode → ""/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE\.md""\nhighest tier · cannot be excluded" as POLICY <<app>>
}
node "Agent home (written by the seed)" as HOME <<host>> {
  file "opencode → ""\.config/opencode/AGENTS\.md""" as USERFILE <<app>>
}
folder "Operator's repository" as REPO <<error>>

component "**route** — ""_house_rules_target""\none row per supported harness" as ROUTE <<app>>
component "**write** — ""_proveo_write_block""\nmarked region only" as WRITE <<app>>
component "agent — merges user + project" as AGENT <<app>>

SRC ARROW_MAIN POLICY : baked at BUILD time (uid 0)
SRC ARROW_MAIN ROUTE
ROUTE ARROW_MAIN WRITE : only where a user-level file EXISTS
WRITE ARROW_MAIN USERFILE
POLICY ARROW_MAIN AGENT : loaded FIRST, every session
USERFILE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : loaded every session
REPO ARROW_MAIN AGENT : project rules, ranked HIGHER
ROUTE ARROW_ERROR REPO : never written to

note bottom of REPO
  **The workspace is not ours to seed.** Writing an AGENTS\.md there mutates the
  operator's checkout, competes with one they already wrote, and cannot apply at
  all when theirs exists. The USER layer has none of those problems: both
  harnesses below MERGE it with the project's instead of choosing, and both rank
  the project's higher — so a repo can always overrule the house.
end note

note right of ROUTE
  **Every supported harness gets a row, including the empty ones**, so silence is
  a decision a reader can check rather than an oversight.

  ""claudecode"" NOT here — ""/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE\.md"", baked by the Dockerfile.
              The MANAGED POLICY tier loads before the user and project files and
              cannot be excluded by ""claudeMdExcludes"" at any settings layer,
              which is what "always applies" actually requires. The home file
              this table writes is the LOWEST tier, and a project CLAUDE\.md
              outranks it — so it could not have guaranteed anything.
  ""opencode""   ~/\.config/opencode/AGENTS\.md — the documented global file;
              instructions render global first, then project on top.
  ""cursor""     NONE. cursor-agent reads ""\.cursor/rules"" and a project-root
              AGENTS\.md/CLAUDE\.md; its global "User Rules" live in the IDE
              settings UI, not a file the CLI reads.
  ""cecli""      NONE established. It seeds a PROJECT CONVENTIONS\.md from its own
              defaults; guessing a user-level path writes a file nothing reads.
end note

note bottom of WRITE
  The destination may already hold hand-written content, so the region proveo
  owns is delimited by HTML comment markers and everything outside them is
  copied through untouched. The block is REPLACED on every start rather than
  appended, which is what keeps a long-lived proveo home from growing a new copy
  per run. ""PROVEO_HOUSE_RULES=off"" skips the whole step.
end note

note top of SRC
  Baked into the image rather than mounted: it must be present on BOTH backends,
  and a file the sandbox cannot edit cannot be edited by the agent either.
end note

' ── 7g. UI defaults — claudecode only ────────────────────────────────────────
file "/opt/proveo/themes/proveo-sandbox\.json\nbaked, proveo's identity palette" as THEME <<db>>
component "**apply** — ""proveo_apply_ui_defaults""\n""PROVEO_UI_DEFAULTS=off"" skips it" as UIFN <<app>>
file """~/\.claude/settings\.json""\nthe operator's file — merged, never written" as SETTINGS <<app>>
component "a sandbox session indistinguishable\nfrom a host one" as MIXUP <<error>>

THEME ARROW_MAIN UIFN : copied to ""~/\.claude/themes/""
UIFN ARROW_MAIN SETTINGS : ""theme"" · ""syntaxHighlightingDisabled""
SETTINGS ARROW_MAIN AGENT : read every session
UIFN ARROW_ERROR MIXUP : the thing it exists to prevent

note bottom of UIFN
  **A sandboxed session and a host session are
  the same program in the same terminal.** With
  nothing to tell them apart, a command meant
  for the sandbox gets typed into the host — so
  the accent goes cyan, not the default orange.
end note

note right of THEME
  **Baked, then copied by the seed.** A theme is
  JSON at ""~/\.claude/themes/<slug>\.json"",
  selected as ""custom:<slug>"" — so shipping one
  in the image reaches both backends without a
  network fetch or an operator step.
end note

note bottom of SETTINGS
  **MERGED, and only where the key is absent.**
  The file is the operator's; proveo sets
  ""theme"" and ""syntaxHighlightingDisabled"" and
  nothing else, and the cwd guard's PreToolUse
  hook merges into this same file.
end note

note right of SETTINGS
  **The default is what an inherited file can
  quietly flip.** Syntax highlighting is already
  Claude Code's default, so it is written down
  explicitly — a grep result rendered as flat
  text is materially harder to read.
end note
@enduml
